  "aboutPageTitle": "About",
  "aboutTabIntroLabel": "Intro",
  "aboutTabIntroHeroTitle": "Understand How Your Data Is Stored, Used, and Taken With You",
  "aboutTabIntroHeroBody": "Quill Diary is a local, encrypted journal that does not require its own account. Everyday writing and search work offline; you decide when to create external copies or use Google Drive and AI services.",
  "aboutTabIntroChip0": "Data Encryption",
  "aboutTabIntroChip1": "No Sign-Up",
  "aboutTabIntroChip2": "Full-Text Search",
  "aboutTabIntroChip3": "Backup & Export",
  "aboutTabIntroSection0Title": "Why It Works Well for Journaling",
  "aboutTabIntroSection0Subtitle": "Data storage and everyday features are both designed around private personal journaling.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection0Item0Title": "Encrypted Local Storage",
  "aboutTabIntroSection0Item0Body": "Entries, attachments, people, drafts, and the search index stay encrypted on your device by default. Recovery settings, the tag catalog, pinned-item IDs, and other supporting data are not separately encrypted, but remain in private app storage.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection0Item1Title": "Start without Signing Up",
  "aboutTabIntroSection0Item1Body": "You do not need a Quill Diary account. Set up a recovery key on first use to start reading and writing entries. You only link a Google account within the app when using Google Drive backup and restore.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection0Item2Title": "Less Collection, Less Distraction",
  "aboutTabIntroSection0Item2Body": "The app contains no advertising or tracking SDKs and does not upload plaintext diaries to developer-controlled servers. AI chat sends conversations, prompts and images directly to your chosen provider. Diary organization sends only this entry’s masked body and organization chat, without images or attachments. Entering its chat makes no AI request; discuss your requirements before generating a draft. API keys stay in on-device secure storage and are excluded from backups. Services, URLs and prompts are encrypted in the vault and included in full backups. Providers retain received data according to their own policies.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Title": "How You Can Use It",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Subtitle": "From capturing the moment to reviewing later, common features are designed around personal journaling.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item0Title": "Write What You Want to Remember",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item0Body": "Supports titles, dates, tags, images, and general attachments. Start writing a new entry immediately or read before editing an existing one. Export to Markdown or HTML when needed.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item1Title": "View Your Entries from Different Angles",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item1Body": "The home screen offers list, calendar, tag, people, and overview views. Browse by time, revisit by date, or organize your life through tags, people, and stats.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item2Title": "Find What You Wrote Before",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item2Body": "Once unlocked, you can search titles, tags, and body text by keyword to find an experience or something you mentioned.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item3Title": "Backups and Exports Serve Different Purposes",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item3Body": "A full backup restores the entire saved vault. Markdown or HTML is suited to reading and organizing content outside the app.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item4Title": "Make the App Fit You",
  "aboutTabIntroSection1Item4Body": "In Personalization, you can adjust the interface language, light or dark theme, auto-lock timing, image quality, and diary typography. Image quality affects only new images added through the regular editor, not chat attachments.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection2Title": "You Stay in Control of Your Data",
  "aboutTabIntroSection2Subtitle": "Backup, export, and unlock methods play different roles so you can keep your data and understand the risk boundaries.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection2Item0Title": "Trusted Device and Recovery Key",
  "aboutTabIntroSection2Item0Body": "Screen lock and biometrics make everyday access convenient. A recovery key unlocks the original vault or its full backup, but the key itself does not contain your entries.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection2Item1Title": "Full Backups Restore the Vault",
  "aboutTabIntroSection2Item1Body": "A full backup preserves saved entries, attachments, people, and other vault data for a complete restore. It is not a directly readable export document.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection2Item2Title": "Protect Exported Content Yourself",
  "aboutTabIntroSection2Item2Body": "Markdown and HTML exports are good for reading, organizing, and moving content, but they are readable documents and are no longer protected like in-app encrypted storage.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection3Title": "Open Source and Branding",
  "aboutTabIntroSection3Subtitle": "Review the source code and license terms, and understand branding boundaries clearly.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection3Item0Title": "Open Source Under AGPL-3.0-or-later",
  "aboutTabIntroSection3Item0Body": "Source code is released under AGPL-3.0-or-later for public review. Android is currently the only supported platform.",
  "aboutTabIntroSection3Item1Title": "Quill Diary Branding",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionLabel": "Unlock & Security",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionHeroTitle": "Everyday Unlock and Emergency Recovery Serve Different Purposes",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionHeroBody": "Screen lock and biometrics handle everyday re-verification. A recovery key restores a backup or regains access after device trust is lost. Changing phones still requires a full backup; your device PIN and biometrics cannot replace the recovery key.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionChip0": "Recovery Key",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionChip1": "Biometrics",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionChip2": "Screen Lock",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionChip3": "Auto-Lock",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Title": "Choosing an Unlock Method",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Subtitle": "Choose the unlock method in Settings based on your device habits and desired protection level.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Item0Title": "None",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Item0Body": "After a background-timeout lock, access resumes without system verification. After manual lock, you still need to tap Re-verify. This is convenient but offers the least protection.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Item1Title": "Device Screen Lock",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Item1Body": "Re-verify with PIN, pattern, or password when returning to the app. Good if you want system-level protection without relying on biometrics.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Item2Title": "Biometrics",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Item2Body": "Prefer fingerprint or face verification. Depending on the device and system prompt, screen lock may be offered as a fallback. This is usually the most convenient daily option.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Item3Title": "Shared Requirements",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection0Item3Body": "Screen lock and biometric modes require a device screen lock first. Biometrics must also be enrolled in system settings.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Title": "When Re-Verification Happens",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Subtitle": "Entries, drafts, attachments, and search data are available only during a valid unlocked session.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item0Title": "During a Valid Unlocked Session",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item0Body": "Once unlocked, you can read and write entries, edit drafts, add attachments, and search. Until a recovery key is created, diary content remains unavailable even if the home screen is visible.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item1Title": "Background Timeout",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item2Title": "When Returning to the App",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item2Body": "A brief app switch usually does not trigger immediate re-verification. After a longer background stay, your chosen mode decides whether to verify again. Locking only pauses access; it does not delete your entries.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item3Title": "After Cancelled or Failed Verification",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item3Body": "If verification is cancelled or unsuccessful, the app stays locked and stops retrying automatically. Tap Re-verify when you want to try again.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item4Title": "After Manual Lock",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection1Item4Body": "After manual lock from Settings, return to the app and tap Re-verify. It will not unlock automatically.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection2Title": "Why a Recovery Key Is Still Needed",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection2Subtitle": "Device verification makes everyday unlocking convenient. Changing phones or reinstalling requires a full backup and its matching recovery key.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection2Item0Title": "Everyday Unlocking Cannot Replace Backup and Recovery",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection2Item0Body": "After changing phones or clearing app data, obtain a full backup first, then restore it with the recovery key saved when that backup was created. The old PIN, pattern, password, or biometrics cannot replace the backup or recovery key.",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection2Item1Title": "Store It Safely",
  "aboutTabUnlockSessionSection2Item1Body": "A recovery key can restore access to its matching vault or full backup, but it does not contain your entries. Losing it may make recovery impossible, so keep a separate copy in a safe place.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionLabel": "Data Encryption",
  "aboutTabEncryptionHeroTitle": "Protect Journal Content Before It Is Stored",
  "aboutTabEncryptionHeroBody": "Saved entries, attachments, people, drafts, and search data are stored encrypted and can be read or written only during a valid unlocked session. Plaintext exports and an unlocked device still need your protection.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionChip0": "File Encryption",
  "aboutTabEncryptionChip1": "Security Checks",
  "aboutTabEncryptionChip2": "Key Protection",
  "aboutTabEncryptionChip3": "Recovery Key",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection0Title": "What This Protection Does for You",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection0Subtitle": "Content is encrypted before it is stored and opened through the current valid unlocked session when needed.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection0Item0Title": "Encrypted Sensitive Content",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection0Item0Body": "Saved entries, attachments, people, and drafts use the LDJ2 container format with AES-256-GCM content encryption. Even with the files, their contents cannot be read directly.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection0Item1Title": "Stop When Tampering Is Detected",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection0Item1Body": "Encrypted files are integrity-checked. If their contents or headers are modified, decryption fails instead of treating unverifiable data as normal content.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection0Item2Title": "Different Files Use Different Keys",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection0Item2Body": "LDJ2 files, such as entries and attachments, each use an independently generated content key, rather than sharing one file key across all content.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection1Title": "How You Open Your Own Data",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection1Subtitle": "Everyday and emergency paths differ, but both end in the same decryption flow.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection1Item0Title": "Trusted Device",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection1Item0Body": "A trusted device uses screen lock, biometrics, or no additional authentication, depending on your chosen mode. The material used to decrypt the vault is protected by built-in device security.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection1Item1Title": "Recovery Key",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection1Item1Body": "When restoring a full backup or recovering after device trust is lost, the recovery key can restore access. Argon2id first derives the wrapping key used to protect the vault. The recovery key itself does not contain your entries.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection1Item2Title": "Verify the Vault First, Then Open Each File",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection1Item2Body": "The app confirms that you can enter the vault before opening its files, avoiding a wrong key being mistaken for damaged data.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection2Title": "Boundaries to Understand",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection2Subtitle": "Content is encrypted, but headers, recovery settings, and some supporting data remain readable, including the tag catalog and pinned-item IDs. Plaintext exports and unlocked use also need care.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection2Item0Title": "Exports Use a Different Protection Layer",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection2Item0Body": "Once you export to Markdown or HTML, storage and sharing risks for readable documents are no longer handled by in-app encryption.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection2Item1Title": "Keep Your Recovery Key Safe",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection2Item1Body": "The recovery key is essential for re-entering the vault. If it leaks, is lost, or is not stored safely, security and recoverability may be affected.",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection2Item2Title": "Protect the Device While Unlocked",
  "aboutTabEncryptionSection2Item2Body": "Encryption mainly protects stored data. Viewing or editing attachments may create readable temporary files. Someone with access to an unlocked app or compromised device may still read content that is currently available.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexLabel": "Search",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexHeroTitle": "Find Memories Across Titles, Tags, and Entry Text",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexHeroBody": "Once unlocked, you can search saved entries by keyword. If newly edited content is missing, first check whether you have formally saved it.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexChip0": "Titles, Tags & Body",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexChip1": "Encrypted Index",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexChip2": "Available While Unlocked",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexChip3": "Rebuildable",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection0Title": "What Search Helps You Find",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection0Subtitle": "Useful when reviewing, organizing, or narrowing down a memory quickly.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection0Item0Title": "Search Titles, Tags, and Body Text",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection0Item0Body": "Search keywords in titles, body text, and tags without scrolling through every entry.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection0Item1Title": "The Index Itself Is Protected",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection0Item1Body": "The search index file is encrypted at rest. The app opens and queries its search data only after the vault is unlocked.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection1Title": "How the Index Speeds Up Search",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection1Subtitle": "Lookup work goes to the index layer instead of scanning every saved entry each time.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection1Item0Title": "Index for Speed",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection1Item0Body": "When you enter a keyword, the app queries the search index instead of decrypting the entire vault entry by entry.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection1Item1Title": "Updates Only After Save",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection1Item1Body": "The index updates only after a successful save or import, so results do not mix in drafts.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection1Item2Title": "Can Be Rebuilt When Needed",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection1Item2Body": "The search index is rebuildable derived data. The app rebuilds it after format changes, backup restore, or whenever the existing index cannot be reused.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection2Title": "How It Relates to Security",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection2Subtitle": "Useful search does not mean giving up protection boundaries.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection2Item0Title": "Available Only While Unlocked",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection2Item0Body": "The index is built, updated, and used only while unlocked; it closes when the app locks.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection2Item1Title": "If Recent Edits Are Missing",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection2Item1Body": "Search shows only entries formally saved to the vault. If a recent addition or edit is missing, first confirm that you finished saving that entry.",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection2Item2Title": "The Vault Remains the Source of Truth",
  "aboutTabSearchIndexSection2Item2Body": "The search index only helps you find content quickly. Saved entries in the encrypted vault remain the source of truth.",
  "aboutTabEditorLabel": "Writing",
  "aboutTabEditorHeroTitle": "Capture the Moment, Then Choose When to Save It",
  "aboutTabEditorHeroBody": "Edits are first kept as encrypted drafts, with a reminder when they are not formally saved. When ready, save them to the vault and organize the entry with tags, checklists, images, and attachments, or use AI to write from a chat or organize an existing entry.",
  "aboutTabEditorChip0": "Auto Drafts",
  "aboutTabEditorChip1": "Task Lists",
  "aboutTabEditorChip2": "Images & Files",
  "aboutTabEditorChip3": "Markdown Editing",
  "aboutTabEditorChip4": "AI",
  "aboutTabEditorAiSectionTitle": "AI Features",
  "aboutTabEditorAiSectionSubtitle": "Talk with AI and turn the conversation into an entry, or organize an existing entry. Both are written to the vault only after you confirm.",
  "aboutTabEditorAiItem0Title": "Chat Diary",
  "aboutTabEditorAiItem0Body": "When creating an entry, you can write directly or chat with AI. A draft is created only after you generate it from the current conversation, and it is saved to the vault only after you confirm. Unfinished chats appear on the home screen; after saving, you can reopen the retained conversation from that entry. Conversations, prompts, and images go directly to the provider you configure.",
  "aboutTabEditorAiItem1Title": "Diary Organization",
  "aboutTabEditorAiItem1Body": "Open organization from the AI button on a saved entry. Mark text you do not want to send, then discuss how to revise it. Opening the chat does not call AI immediately. After you organize, one draft is created; the body updates only after you review the differences and confirm. The title, date, tags, and attachments stay the same. Only this entry’s masked body and the current conversation are sent, and it does not send images or attachments.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Title": "Everyday Writing Features",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Subtitle": "Built around personal records, with common organization tools split into clearer parts of the same editing flow.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item0Title": "Create or Edit Existing Entries",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item0Body": "New entries open in edit mode; saved entries can be read before switching to edit.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item1Title": "Content, Title, and Date",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item1Body": "Edit the title, date, time, and body. Saving requires at least a title or body so the diary does not accumulate blank entries.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item2Title": "Tags",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item2Body": "Create, select, and organize tags, and use colors to distinguish them. Browse from the Tags view later or search the tag text directly.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item3Title": "Task Lists",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item3Body": "Add task lists within your writing, check items, and continue editing normally. Checkboxes also remain interactive in preview.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item4Title": "Images and General Attachments",
  "aboutTabEditorSection0Item4Body": "You can add multiple images or general files and reorder images. The image-quality setting in Personalization affects only new images added through the regular editor. GIFs keep their original files, chat attachments do not use this setting, and existing attachments are not reprocessed.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection1Title": "Draft System",
  "aboutTabEditorSection1Subtitle": "Automatic drafts reduce the risk of losing changes when writing is interrupted.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection1Item0Title": "Changes Are Auto-Saved",
  "aboutTabEditorSection1Item0Body": "After entering edit mode, changes auto-save as encrypted drafts to reduce loss if interrupted.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection1Item1Title": "Restore When Reopening",
  "aboutTabEditorSection1Item1Body": "When you reopen a regular entry or unfinished new entry, the app asks whether you want to continue if a local draft is still available. Diaries generated from chat load their drafts directly.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection1Item2Title": "Auto Cleanup After Save",
  "aboutTabEditorSection1Item2Body": "Once content is successfully saved to the vault, its draft is cleared. Closing the editor and choosing to discard changes also deletes that draft.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection2Title": "Relationship to Other Data",
  "aboutTabEditorSection2Subtitle": "In-progress edits stay separate from saved content, and the app shows when a local draft still needs attention.",
  "aboutTabEditorSection2Item0Title": "Unsaved Indicator",
  "aboutTabEditorSection2Item0Body": "If an entry still has a local draft, list and view modes show an unsaved marker reminding you that the content has not been saved yet.",
  "aboutTabPeopleLabel": "People Directory",
  "aboutTabPeopleHeroTitle": "Connect Related Memories Through Names and Aliases",
  "aboutTabPeopleHeroBody": "Save names, aliases, relationships, and notes, then insert a person's name quickly while writing. The app organizes mentions and related saved entries without rewriting your original text.",
  "aboutTabPeopleChip0": "Quick @ Insert",
  "aboutTabPeopleChip1": "Names & Aliases",
  "aboutTabPeopleChip2": "Mentioned Entries",
  "aboutTabPeopleChip3": "Relationships & Notes",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection0Title": "Create and Organize People",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection0Subtitle": "Keep the details that help identify each person and describe your relationship.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection0Item0Title": "Names and Aliases",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection0Item0Body": "Create a person with their main name and add nicknames or other names. When renaming someone, keep the old name as an alias so past entries can still be recognized.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection0Item1Title": "Relationships and Familiarity",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection0Item1Body": "Record one or more relationships, add a description and familiarity level, then use a color and notes as helpful reminders.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection0Item2Title": "Birthday and Year Met",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection0Item2Body": "Optionally record the month and day of a birthday and the year you met to preserve important moments in the relationship.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection1Title": "Revisit Your Shared Stories",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection1Subtitle": "When you use People, the app updates rebuildable mention insights from names and aliases so related records are easier to review.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection1Item0Title": "Recognize Names and Aliases",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection1Item0Body": "The app matches a person's main name and aliases against titles and content in encrypted search data instead of decrypting the entire vault entry by entry each time.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection1Item1Title": "Review Mentions and Entries",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection1Item1Body": "A person's page shows the number of entries mentioning them, entries from the past 30 days, the most recent mention date, and related entries. The people list can also be sorted using these details. Multiple mentions in one entry still count as one entry.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection1Item2Title": "Insert a Name Quickly with @",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection1Item2Body": "Type @ in the entry editor to choose a person and insert their chosen diary name (the main name by default, or an alias you pick). It remains ordinary text and does not turn the entry into a special format.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection2Title": "Good to Know",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection2Subtitle": "People helps organize your diary without replacing or rewriting saved content.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection2Item0Title": "Insights Use Saved Entries",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection2Item0Body": "Mention insights use saved entries only; drafts appear after they are saved. The derived insights are excluded from full backups and can be rebuilt after restore.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection2Item1Title": "Deleting a Person Keeps Your Entries",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection2Item1Body": "Deleting a person removes only their profile and related insights. It does not delete or rewrite any entry; the names and text you originally wrote remain.",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection2Item2Title": "Clearer Names Match Better",
  "aboutTabPeopleSection2Item2Body": "Very short, identical, or overlapping names and aliases can cause incorrect matches. Names that clearly distinguish people make mention insights and related entries more accurate.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreLabel": "Backup & Restore",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreHeroTitle": "Restore on a New Phone, or Import and Export Entries",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreHeroBody": "A full backup preserves the entire saved vault. Markdown and HTML exports let you select content for reading or external use. Importing entries adds content, while a full restore replaces the current saved vault.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreChip0": "Full Backup",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreChip1": "Google Drive",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreChip2": "Import & Export",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreChip3": "Markdown / HTML",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Title": "Changing Phones or Reinstalling the App",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Subtitle": "Prepare the original recovery key and a fresh backup on the old phone. Erase the old device only after verifying the restore on the new one.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Item0Title": "Prepare the Old Phone First",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Item0Body": "Formally save any drafts you need, confirm that the original recovery key is available, then create a fresh full backup and wait for the success message. Keep the old phone and backup until the restore is verified.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Item1Title": "Transfer With an External ZIP",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Item1Body": "On the old phone, choose Export Backup to Folder and safely move the backup_*.zip file to the new phone. Then choose Import External Backup in Settings on the new phone. Do not use Import Entries for this file.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Item2Title": "Transfer With Google Drive",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Item2Body": "On the old phone, link your Google Account and finish Back Up to Google Drive. After initial setup on the new phone, link the same account and choose Restore From Google Drive. Drive backup is manual and does not live-sync the two phones.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Item3Title": "Verify Before Erasing the Old Phone",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection0Item3Body": "If asked for a key, enter the recovery key saved when the old backup was created, not a key newly generated on the new phone. Verify entries, attachments, people, tags, and pinned items before resetting or erasing the old phone.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Title": "When to Use Full Backup",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Subtitle": "If you want to preserve the entire main vault and restore it later as-is, use full backup.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Item0Title": "Preserve the Complete Vault",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Item0Body": "A full backup includes saved entries, attachments, people, retained conversations from completed chats, recovery settings, and the encrypted AI service, URL, and prompts. Content files stay encrypted, but the ZIP container, recovery settings, and any tag catalog or pinned-item IDs are not separately encrypted.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Item1Title": "Verified After Creation",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Item1Body": "Full backups are structurally verified before delivery to local storage, external folders, or Google Drive.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Item2Title": "Retention Count",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Item2Body": "Local backups and Google Drive keep the latest {retainCount} copies. Exports to external folders are not automatically rotated or deleted.",
  "@aboutTabBackupRestoreSection1Item2Body": {
    "placeholders": {
      "retainCount": {
        "type": "int"
      }
    }
  },
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection2Title": "What Happens During Restore",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection2Subtitle": "Restore does not patch missing entries. It replaces the current main vault with the backup copy.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection2Item0Title": "The Main Vault Is Overwritten",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection2Item0Body": "Whether the backup comes from the in-app list, an external ZIP, or Google Drive, restore replaces the current saved vault with the backup contents.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection2Item1Title": "The Search Index Is Rebuilt",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection2Item1Body": "Search data is rebuilt after restore, and you may need to verify again. On the same device with a valid unlocked session, you may sometimes continue directly.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection2Item2Title": "Recovery Key May Be Required",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection2Item2Body": "If trusted status on this device cannot directly match that backup, the flow asks for the recovery key saved when the backup was created.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection3Title": "Import and Export",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection3Subtitle": "Portable documents let you take out, read, or add selected entries without restoring the entire vault.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection3Item0Title": "Import Entries",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection3Item0Body": "Import Entries handles Markdown, HTML, folders, supported portable ZIP files, and Easy Diary backups. Quill Diary full-backup ZIP files must use Import External Backup instead; the two flows are not interchangeable.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection3Item1Title": "Export Readable Documents",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection3Item1Body": "Both Markdown and HTML let you select specific entries. A Markdown ZIP preserves separate files and attachments for easier re-import, while HTML arranges the content in a single file for direct reading.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection4Title": "Check Before Exporting",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection4Subtitle": "Choose the entries you need, then check the exported content, privacy options, and where you will save the file.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection4Item0Title": "Choose Entries to Export",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection4Item0Body": "Markdown and HTML exports let you choose specific entries. Import Entries previews a supported file and lets you choose content before creating new entries. Imported content may duplicate existing entries and does not sync with the source file.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection4Item1Title": "Reduce Identifying Information First",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection4Item1Body": "Markdown and HTML can replace names and aliases from your People list with labels by enabling Hide Person Names. HTML can also exclude images and attachments. These options only reduce some identification risks.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection4Item2Title": "Review Before Using External Tools",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection4Item2Body": "Hide Person Names only replaces names and aliases registered in your People list. Unlisted names and other clues in titles, tags, dates, places, or event details may still identify someone. Exported files are plaintext, so review them yourself first. After delivery, use, retention, and deletion follow the policies of your chosen tool.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection5Title": "Things to Know Before Use",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection5Subtitle": "Backups and exports both create copies, but their protection and restore purposes differ.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection5Item0Title": "Drafts and device preferences are not backed up",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection5Item0Body": "Full backups exclude regular editing drafts, unfinished chats, diary organization sessions, API keys and device preferences such as language, theme, auto-lock, image quality and diary typography. Organization chats, hidden selections and the candidate under review are encrypted locally and the unaccepted candidate is cleared on returning to chat, and the session is cleared after applying or confirming deletion. Restoring also clears local drafts and pending attachments.",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection5Item1Title": "Backup and Import/Export Are Not Sync",
  "aboutTabBackupRestoreSection5Item1Body": "Google Drive is a place to manually create and restore full backups, not to sync entries live. Imported entries and their source files are independent, so later changes do not automatically update the other copy.",
  "legalBrandDisclaimer": "The Quill Diary name, icon, and Google Play Store listing are author branding and are not transferred with the code license.",
